@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# 10. Fixed ticket due times
+
+Date: 2026-11-15
+Status: Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+The help desk promises response times and must enable them after existing data is ready, with rollback to 1.4.0 available.
+
+## Decision
+
+The store assigns each ticket a fixed ISO `due` time from creation plus configured priority hours. The persistence record explicitly keeps the optional field in version 1. Startup backfills missing values and saves before serving requests, even when exposure is off. Existing values are never recomputed. No audit or notification is generated for backfill.
+
+Only `DUE_TIMES=on` exposes due and activates overdue filtering; default responses remain unchanged. Overdue means an active ticket whose deadline is strictly before the injected clock, and filtering precedes pagination. Imports use the same configured hours.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Release 1.4.0 ignores the added fields and still reads every ticket. Its writes drop unknown fields; operators retain a backup for a later upgrade. Raw output preserves all existing column positions and appends due only when enabled.
